  "description": "Out-of-process database capture for Kronikol: a byte-for-byte TCP tee that sits between a service and Redis or MongoDB, forwards every byte unmodified and first, decodes a copy of the wire protocol (RESP2/RESP3, MongoDB OP_MSG/OP_QUERY) off the hot path, and records each command/reply as a Kronikol request/response pair. Renders out-of-process Redis and Mongo calls in sequence diagrams exactly like the in-process Kronikol.Extensions.Redis / Kronikol.Extensions.MongoDB extensions, with no change inside the service.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
